  "notes": "Released 2026-08-15. Desktop proxy recovery now follows the operating\nsystem's observed state and keeps recovery evidence whenever cleanup is not\nconclusively complete.\n\n## Reliability and security\n\n- The desktop client clears its crash-recovery marker only after a fresh\n  operating-system read proves that HTTP, HTTPS, and SOCKS proxies are all\n  disabled. Failed, timed-out, partial, ambiguous, or localized responses\n  remain recoverable on the next launch.\n- macOS checks every network service, while KDE reads the active\n  `kioslaverc` backend instead of an unrelated settings source.\n- `github.com/klauspost/compress` is updated to 1.18.7, which includes the\n  upstream fix for GO-2026-5841.\n- Regression coverage now includes command failures, timeouts, duplicate or\n  unknown status fields, and cold-start recovery retries.\n",
